# Automatisch (`automatisch-automatisch`)

Transform your business with Automatisch, the open-source automation tool that seamlessly connects apps like Twitter, Slack, and more. Enhance efficiency and maintain data control with ease and flexibility.

[Service documentation](https://docs.osaas.io/osaas.wiki/Service%3A-Automatisch.html) · [Source](https://github.com/automatisch/automatisch)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "automatisch-automatisch"
  name       = "myautomatisch"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    RedisUrl = var.redis_url
    PostgresUrl = var.postgres_url
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `RedisUrl` | string | yes | Redis server address as redis://host:port (env REDIS_URL), e.g. redis://redis.example.com:6379. The OSC entrypoint splits it into REDIS_HOST and REDIS_PORT, so credentials and database path are not supported; defaults to localhost:6379 if unset. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `PostgresUrl` | string | yes | PostgreSQL connection URL in the form postgres://username:password@host:port/database (env POSTGRES_URL), e.g. postgres://automatisch:secret@db.example.com:5432/automatisch. The OSC entrypoint splits it into the POSTGRES_* variables Automatisch reads. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
